      "status": "passed",
      "reason": "Each domain lists source type (academic study, journalist report, case study) with approximate date/scope and unverified marker.",
      "evidence_ids": []
    },
    "Check that mechanisms and direction/magnitude are stated per domain": {
      "status": "passed",
      "reason": "Each domain includes at least one concrete mechanism and direction/magnitude statement, with unknown magnitude flagged where applicable.",
      "evidence_ids": []
    }
  },
  "ledger": {
    "requirements": [
      "Analyze social media's impact across key domains (communication, politics, mental health, economy, education, social cohesion)",
      "For each domain, evaluate both positive and negative effects",
      "Use evidence from academic studies, journalist reports, and case studies",
      "For each domain, state evidence source type and approximate date/scope, labeled unverified in this run",
      "For each domain, provide at least one concrete mechanism and direction/magnitude",
      "Distinguish empirical evidence from interpretation",
      "Publish compact domain analyses to shared ledger"
    ],
    "outline": [
      "COMMUNICATION: Positive - global connectivity, low-cost reach. Negative - echo chambers, misinformation spread. Evidence: academic studies (e.g., Pew Research surveys 2010s-2020s, unverified); journalist reports (e.g., NYT/Guardian coverage of misinformation, unverified). Mechanism: algorithmic curation reinforces homophily, increasing exposure to like-minded content. Direction: positive for connectivity (large magnitude), negative for information quality (moderate magnitude). Uncertainty: magnitude of echo chamber effect debated.",
      "COMMUNICATION (cont): Case study - Facebook's role in Myanmar/Rohingya violence (2017, journalist reports, unverified) shows amplification of hate speech. Mechanism: platform algorithms prioritize engagement, spreading inflammatory content. Direction: negative, large magnitude in conflict settings. Uncertainty: causal attribution complex; platform policies changed since.",
      "POLITICS: Positive - civic engagement, protest mobilization (e.g., Arab Spring 2010-2012, academic/journalist, unverified). Negative - polarization, foreign interference (e.g., 2016 US election, academic studies, unverified). Mechanism: targeted ads and bots amplify divisive messages. Direction: positive for mobilization (moderate), negative for democratic quality (moderate-large). Uncertainty: causal effects on polarization contested.",
      "POLITICS (cont): Case study - Cambridge Analytica (2018, journalist reports, unverified) shows data misuse for political targeting. Mechanism: psychographic profiling enables micro-targeting. Direction: negative, moderate magnitude. Uncertainty: actual electoral impact unclear.",
      "MENTAL HEALTH: Positive - social support, reduced isolation for marginalized groups (e.g., LGBTQ+ youth, academic studies 2010s, unverified). Negative - increased depression/anxiety among adolescents (e.g., Twenge 2017, academic, unverified). Mechanism: social comparison and cyberbullying. Direction: negative for adolescents (moderate), positive for support (moderate). Uncertainty: evidence thin/contradictory; effect sizes small, causality debated.",
      "MENTAL HEALTH (cont): Case study - Instagram internal research (2021, journalist reports, unverified) suggests body image issues in teen girls. Mechanism: idealized content exposure. Direction: negative, moderate. Uncertainty: leaked documents, not peer-reviewed; company disputes.",
      "ECONOMY: Positive - e-commerce growth, gig economy jobs (e.g., Upwork/Etsy, journalist reports 2010s-2020s, unverified). Negative - market concentration, data exploitation (e.g., Facebook/Google ad duopoly, academic studies, unverified). Mechanism: network effects create winner-take-all markets. Direction: positive for consumer access (moderate), negative for competition (moderate). Uncertainty: net economic effect unclear.",
      "ECONOMY (cont): Case study - Facebook's ad revenue model (2010s, journalist reports, unverified) shows data-driven targeting. Mechanism: user data monetization. Direction: negative for privacy, positive for business efficiency. Uncertainty: magnitude of harm vs. benefit not quantified.",
      "EDUCATION: Positive - access to information, online learning (e.g., Khan Academy, MOOC platforms, academic studies 2010s, unverified). Negative - distraction, reduced deep reading (e.g., Carr's 'The Shallows' 2010, journalist/academic, unverified). Mechanism: notification-driven attention fragmentation. Direction: positive for access (moderate), negative for cognitive depth (moderate). Uncertainty: long-term effects on learning outcomes unclear.",
      "EDUCATION (cont): Case study - COVID-19 remote learning (2020-2021, journalist reports, unverified) shows both benefits and learning loss. Mechanism: platform access vs. digital divide. Direction: mixed; negative for disadvantaged students (moderate). Uncertainty: pandemic-specific, not generalizable.",
      "SOCIAL COHESION: Positive - community building, cross-cultural exchange (e.g., diaspora groups, academic studies 2010s, unverified). Negative - polarization, hate speech (e.g., Parler/4chan case studies, journalist reports, unverified). Mechanism: algorithmic amplification of outrage. Direction: negative for cohesion (moderate), positive for sub-group identity (moderate). Uncertainty: evidence thin/contradictory; net effect unclear.",
      "SOCIAL COHESION (cont): Case study - QAnon conspiracy movement (2020-2021, journalist reports, unverified) shows platform-driven radicalization. Mechanism: recommendation algorithms lead users down rabbit holes. Direction: negative, moderate-large. Uncertainty: causal pathway debated; platform moderation varies."
    ],
    "evidence_spans": [],
    "source_references": []
  }
}

